= pH — Technical =

== Formal chemical definition ==
The IUPAC pH quantity is defined as the negative base-10 logarithm of the dimensionless hydrogen-ion activity:

<pre>
pH = -lg a(H+)
</pre>

For appropriate dilute aqueous approximations, activity can be related to a concentration or molality and an activity coefficient. Replacing activity by the numerical molar concentration is an approximation rather than the formal definition.

== Measurement caveat ==
Single-ion activity cannot be independently determined without conventions, making direct realization of the formal definition impossible. Operational pH scales use standardized procedures and reference solutions, with an uncertainty chain. An electrode result depends on its calibration, reference electrode and sample matrix.

== Equilibria and temperature ==
Acid dissociation, ionic strength, temperature and buffering determine solution behavior. Neutrality and the dissociation of water depend on temperature, so pH 7 must not be presented as universally neutral under all conditions.

